      "title": "Letterboxd review of The Mummy",
      "snippet": "[Letterboxd Review of \"The Mummy\"] The Universal monsters cycle borrowed a lot from the great silent German Expressionists when it came to lighting, set design and atmosphere, so it made a lot of sense to follow-up the success of Dracula and Frankenstein by upgrading The Last Laugh and Metropolis cinematographer Karl Freund to the directors chair, and to give Boris Karloff another tragic, stiff creature to lend his skill for menace and melancholy to. I get why people don’t care for this one as much as the James Whale entries, as outside of its excellent archaeology expedition prologue where the cursed spell book reanimation occ",
